<%#
  "Looking for a specific service?" — the optional post-results refinement.

  Collapsed and phrased as an invitation rather than a question, because this
  replaced a quiz step that asked the same thing up front. Asking everybody to
  name a service before seeing any results made people who don't know the
  vocabulary stop and wonder whether they should; asking here, over results
  they can already see, costs nothing to ignore.

  Options are the services these matches actually offer, with a count, so no
  choice leads to an empty page. Filtering never re-scores anything — see
  SmartMatch::ServiceFilter.

  Reopened automatically whenever a filter is active, so a user who lands on a
  filtered URL can see (and undo) what is being applied. Otherwise its state
  persists across "Show more" clicks, which replace this panel along with the
  cards — see persistent_details_controller.
%>
<% return unless filter.available? %>

<details class="mb-6 bg-white border rounded-lg border-gray-6 group"
         data-controller="persistent-details"
         data-persistent-details-key-value="smart-match-services"
         data-action="toggle->persistent-details#save"
         <%= "open" if filter.active? %>>
  <summary class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 cursor-pointer list-none">
    <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-2">
      <%= t("smart_match.results.service_filter.title") %>
    </span>
    <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
      <% if filter.active? %>
        <span class="px-2 py-1 text-xs font-semibold rounded-full text-blue-dark bg-blue-pale">
          <%= t("smart_match.results.service_filter.selected", count: filter.selected.size) %>
        </span>
      <% end %>
      <span class="text-gray-4 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
    </span>
  </summary>

  <div class="px-5 pt-1 pb-5 border-t border-gray-6">
    <p class="mt-3 mb-4 text-sm text-gray-4">
      <%= t("smart_match.results.service_filter.hint") %>
    </p>

    <%# A GET form inside the results frame: submitting swaps the cards in
        place, and turbo_action advance puts the selection in the URL so it can
        be reloaded, shared and backed out of.

        No page param, so changing the filter returns to the first page rather
        than to page 3 of a result set that no longer has one. %>
    <%= form_with url: smart_match_result_path, method: :get,
                  data: { turbo_action: "advance" } do %>
      <div class="pr-1 space-y-5 overflow-y-auto max-h-80">
        <% filter.options.each do |cause, options| %>
          <fieldset>
            <legend class="mb-2 text-xs font-bold tracking-wide uppercase text-gray-4">
              <%= cause %>
            </legend>

            <%# Selected state is pure CSS (.sm-pill-option:has(input:checked)),
                so ticking a box needs no JavaScript and the control still works
                with Turbo unavailable. %>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <% options.each do |option| %>
                <label class="sm-pill-option inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
                  <input type="checkbox"
                         name="services[]"
                         value="<%= option.name %>"
                         class="sr-only"
                         <%= "checked" if filter.selected.include?(option.name) %> />
                  <span><%= option.name %></span>
                  <span class="text-xs opacity-70"><%= option.count %></span>
                </label>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </fieldset>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 pt-4 mt-4 border-t border-gray-6">
        <button type="submit"
                class="px-6 py-2 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-white uppercase transition-colors rounded-md bg-salmon hover:bg-salmon-medium">
          <%= t("smart_match.results.service_filter.apply") %>
        </button>

        <% if filter.active? %>
          <%= link_to t("smart_match.results.service_filter.clear"),
                smart_match_result_path,
                data: { turbo_action: "advance" },
                class: "text-sm font-semibold underline text-gray-4 hover:text-blue-dark" %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</details>
